Read the class directly and found a real, easy-to-miss behavior worth testing explicitly:
is_trusted() returns TRUE BY DEFAULT when the allowlist is completely empty (no contacts
added yet at all) -- documented in its own docstring as a deliberate "don't silently go quiet
with no indication why" choice. Only once at least one contact exists does it become a real
allowlist. The task's "non-matching sender rejected" case only holds once the list is
non-empty -- tested both states explicitly, not just the non-empty case.

